      "selector": "[class*=\"message\"]",
      "count": 12,
      "outerHTML": "<div class=\"chat-viewer-messages\" id=\"chat-viewer-messages-container\"><div id=\"chat-messages-container\" style=\"position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%; flex: 1 1 0%;\"><div style=\"opacity: 1; transition: opacity 0.2s ease-in; pointer-events: auto;\"><div class=\"chat-user-message-container\"><div class=\"chat-user-message\"><p class=\"whitespace-pre-wrap user-message-content fade-in \" style=\"line-height: 28px;\"><span>hey in this repository I want to create a full on FHIR developer portal for my EHR organization CureMD in .NET and react JS . I want you to copy everything which EPIC's developer portal has and then use it to develop a developer portal for my organization , User CureMD blog websites and login.curemd.com's images and svgs and themese and everytjing like that etc to create a CureMD stylized theme , CureMD FHIR server is a HAPI-FHIR JPA resource server with a Keycloak based Auth server which is extended to be smart on fhir v2 compliant and USCDI v3 complaint . Public documentation of this CureMD server is available at https://www.curemd.com/developer/fhir-apis.pdf  . I also want an EHR launch and standalone launch simulator , During EHR launch first the Application is launched with a SAML assertion of a user name and aspecific client posted on the saml endpoint of keycloak and then the application is launched , this way SSO is established . For the standalone launch , however there are users etc that are logged in which coud be created into the developer portal . The portal should use a keycloak realm to maintain the users , thre shoudl be an admin module and a non admin module , for non admins there should be first a signup screen and then there should be alogin screen , Signup could also be done via google or github accounts via sso and then after signup/login , the users could register apps and then they could develop them launch them etc etc . The admin module shoud be to just managing the applications that have been registered , to upgrade the applicat"
    },
